#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068874 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068677 :question/id #uuid "b107ed10-4501-50ad-8ad7-231fd933bfc9" :question/math-academy-id "e-9997" :question/problem "Rewrite the expression $(x^2 - 12x + 36) -5$ as the difference between a perfect square and a constant." :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the following formula:\n\n$$\nx^2 - {\\color{red}{2}}{\\color{blue}{a}}x + a^2 = (x - {\\color{blue}{a}})^2\n$$\n\nNotice that we have a perfect square in the parentheses that we can factor as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-12x+36 & = \\\\ {x}^{2}-12x+{6}^{2} & = \\\\ {x}^{2}-2\\cdot 6x+{6}^{2} & = \\\\ (x-6{)}^{2} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}^{2}-12x+36)-5 & = \\\\ (x-6{)}^{2}-5 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf9b812d-0dbf-5a67-9d45-3cc5e373b2b1" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069052 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ec0f3923-4b64-5bea-b8d7-55bfc7763001" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x - 6)^{2} - 10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065746} {:answer/id #uuid "4ead1ce6-0411-5bed-85cb-c372af79501e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x + 6)^{2} - 10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065747} {:answer/id #uuid "5cfd603e-809c-520f-90b0-c0b6802486c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x - 12)^{2} - 10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065748} {:answer/id #uuid "6d4c2b1f-aad8-57d7-9575-63cd630f4503" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x - 3)^{2} - 10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065749} {:answer/id #uuid "7edb7a0f-b163-5610-9843-42861214fef8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x + 12)^{2} - 10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065750}] :answer-field/id #uuid "7fa11f12-e4e0-5098-8867-96e3bc8fd3c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186065