 12x + 40.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with ${\\color{red}{2}}$ as a factor:\n\n$$\nx^2 - {\\color{red}{2}}\\cdot {\\color{blue}{6}}x + {\\color{purple}{40}}\n$$\n\nNow, here's the trick. We *add* and *then subtract* ${\\color{blue}{6}}^2,$ writing the constant term ${\\color{purple}{40}}$ last:\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{x^2 - {\\color{red}{2}}\\cdot {\\color{blue}{6}}x + {\\color{blue}{6}}^2} - \\, {\\color{blue}{6}}^2 + {\\color{purple}{40}}\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n(x - {\\color{blue}{6}})^2  - {\\color{blue}{6}}^2 + {\\color{purple}{40}}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n(x - {\\color{blue}{6}})^2  +4.\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "08c6d8d6-3d86-5074-bf99-0cb744c9412a" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069169 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "c4dee27f-94f3-5a51-b01f-76f600699103" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066247} {:answer-field/id #uuid "58e920ba-0b43-533d-b0a9-35bf7f43d663" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066248}] :question/id #uuid "cf79c8bc-0cfa-5bc5-820e-f447e5b11e9c" :question/math-academy-id "q-235904" :question/problem "Complete the square on the quadratic expression $y^{2} - 18y + 64$.$y^{2} - 18y + 64 = ($ {{field-1}} $)^{2} -$\n{{field-2}}"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069189 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c55f4bcc-ccdb-5fb3-99a9-81cf0e13f2e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p =-4, q = 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066336} {:answer/id #uuid "3e0cd0b1-c599-5aa4-860c-0d1885312374" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p =-4, q =-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066337} {:answer/id #uuid "488f232a-a7e6-50aa-9fda-1554ef507144" :answer/type {:db/id